---
// The Cloud skill's showcase: a 7-step engineering-process pipeline —
// business objectives through infrastructure automation — not a comparison
// of the three deployment targets. EKS/K3s/backup still appear, but as
// evidence inside steps 3 and 5, the same way QA's bug report is evidence
// inside a step rather than the card's organizing structure.
//
// Coordinates are deliberately reused, not invented: row 1 is QA's row-1
// geometry (178-wide boxes), row 2 is AI's row-2 geometry (246-wide boxes),
// snaking right at the same drop point AI uses. Same visual language, same
// text budget (see docs — 178w ≈ 22/26 chars, 246w ≈ 30/36 chars).
// Source facts: src/content/cards/cloud.md, docs/context/deployment.md,
// docs/context/decisions.md.
---

<figure class="card-diagram">
  <div class="card-diagram-scroll">
    <svg
      class="topology"
      viewBox="0 0 820 400"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="cloud-pipeline-title cloud-pipeline-desc"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      fill="none"
    >
      <title id="cloud-pipeline-title">Seven steps from business objectives to automated infrastructure</title>
      <desc id="cloud-pipeline-desc">
        One: business and technical objectives, set before any Terraform —
        cost ceilings and a session-scoped production target, because a
        control plane, load balancer and managed cache have no AWS free tier.
        Two: cloud foundation — OIDC-assumed roles instead of long-lived AWS
        keys, and the same least-privilege credential split enforced outside
        AWS entirely. Three: platform environments — EKS, K3s and the
        physical backup each get their own network and DNS, never sharing a
        record. Four: operational guardrails — a nightly auto-destroy is the
        real cost control, since AWS Budgets alerts lag hours; TLS state
        survives a destroyed gateway instead of re-requesting certificates
        into a rate limit. Five: platform resources — a managed cache where
        the design has to prove it survives one, self-hosted Redis where it
        doesn't. Six: platform validation — a silent AWS default caught in
        review before it shipped, not after. Seven: infrastructure
        automation — modular Terraform roots split by lifecycle, shared CI
        actions, and a deploy gate that fails fast when committed infra code
        was never actually applied. From there the flow hands off to the
        DevOps card's release pipeline.
      </desc>

      <defs>
        <marker id="cloud-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path class="arrow-head" d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" stroke="none" />
        </marker>
      </defs>

      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="objectives" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 1, business and technical objectives — open the explanation">
        <rect class="node" x="15" y="40" width="178" height="84" rx="10" />
        <text class="label" x="29" y="64">1 · Objectives</text>
        <text class="sub" x="29" y="82">no free tier, no open bill</text>
        <text class="sub" x="29" y="98">session-scoped by design</text>
      </g>

      <path class="link" d="M193,82 L219,82" marker-end="url(#cloud-arrow)" />

      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="foundation" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 2, cloud foundation — open the explanation">
        <rect class="node" x="219" y="40" width="178" height="84" rx="10" />
        <text class="label" x="233" y="64">2 · Foundation</text>
        <text class="sub" x="233" y="82">OIDC roles, not static keys</text>
        <text class="sub" x="233" y="98">least privilege by policy</text>
      </g>

      <path class="link" d="M397,82 L423,82" marker-end="url(#cloud-arrow)" />

      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="environments" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 3, platform environments — open the explanation">
        <rect class="node" x="423" y="40" width="178" height="84" rx="10" />
        <text class="label" x="437" y="64">3 · Environments</text>
        <text class="sub" x="437" y="82">three networks, one image</text>
        <text class="sub" x="437" y="98">isolated DNS per target</text>
      </g>

      <path class="link" d="M601,82 L627,82" marker-end="url(#cloud-arrow)" />

      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="guardrails" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 4, operational guardrails — open the explanation">
        <rect class="node" x="627" y="40" width="178" height="84" rx="10" />
        <text class="label" x="641" y="64">4 · Guardrails</text>
        <text class="sub" x="641" y="82">auto-destroy, not an alert</text>
        <text class="sub" x="641" y="98">TLS state survives destroy</text>
      </g>

      <path class="link" d="M716,124 L716,230" marker-end="url(#cloud-arrow)" />

      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="resources" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 5, platform resources — open the explanation">
        <rect class="node" x="559" y="230" width="246" height="84" rx="10" />
        <text class="label" x="573" y="254">5 · Platform resources</text>
        <text class="sub" x="573" y="272">managed cache earns its cost</text>
        <text class="sub" x="573" y="288">self-hosted where it doesn't</text>
      </g>

      <path class="link" d="M559,272 L533,272" marker-end="url(#cloud-arrow)" />

      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="validation" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 6, platform validation — open the explanation">
        <rect class="node" x="287" y="230" width="246" height="84" rx="10" />
        <text class="label" x="301" y="254">6 · Platform validation</text>
        <text class="sub" x="301" y="272">a silent AWS default</text>
        <text class="sub" x="301" y="288">caught in review, not after</text>
      </g>

      <path class="link" d="M287,272 L261,272" marker-end="url(#cloud-arrow)" />

      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="automation" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 7, infrastructure automation — open the explanation">
        <rect class="node" x="15" y="230" width="246" height="84" rx="10" />
        <text class="label" x="29" y="254">7 · Infrastructure automation</text>
        <text class="sub" x="29" y="272">modular Terraform, shared CI</text>
        <text class="sub" x="29" y="288">committed isn't applied</text>
      </g>

      <a class="card-jump" href="#card-devops" aria-label="Continue to the DevOps card, where this becomes a deploy pipeline">
        <path class="link" d="M138,314 L138,338" marker-end="url(#cloud-arrow)" />
        <text class="wire" x="150" y="332">ready for DevOps CI/CD</text>
        <text class="wire" x="150" y="346">&amp; application deployment</text>
      </a>

      <text class="wire accent" x="15" y="368">AI compared costs and drafted the trade-off tables</text>
      <text class="wire" x="15" y="384">which one shipped, and which one didn't, was never its call</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="card-diagram-caption">
    Click any step to read what it means.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
